nducted studies on the protective effects of preoperative feeding, highlighting its importance in enhancing patient outcomes in bariatric surgery. His work reflects a commitment to improving surgical practices and patient care in this specialized area of medicine.", "MALTBY JR:Maltby JR is a researcher who has published on fasting and its implications in anesthesia.", "MENDLESON CL:Mendelson CL is a researcher known for his work on aspiration of stomach contents during obstetric anesthesia.", "HUTCHINSON A:Hutchinson A is a researcher who studied gastric fluid volume and pH in elective inpatients.", "HAUSEL J:Hausel J is a researcher who studied the effects of carbohydrate-rich drinks on preoperative discomfort.", "ZELIC M:Zelic M is a researcher who investigated the influence of preoperative oral feeding on stress response after colon cancer resection.", "VAN DEN BERGHE G:Van den Berghe G is a researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the field of intensive insulin therapy, particularly in critically ill patients. His work focuses on the implications of intensive insulin control for nutritional management, highlighting its relevance in improving patient outcomes in critical care settings.", "FINFER S:Finfer S is a researcher who studied glucose control in critically ill patients.", "LJUNGQVIST O:Ljungqvist O is a researcher who has published on preoperative carbohydrate loading and its effects.", "SMITH I:Smith I is a researcher who contributed to the literature on fasting and anesthesia.", "SUBJECTIVE GLOBAL ASSESSMENT:Subjective Global Assessment is a method used to evaluate nutritional status based on clinical judgment. This approach relies on the clinician's expertise to assess an individual's nutritional condition, integrating both subjective and objective data to form a comprehensive evaluation.", "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF ANESTHESIOLOGY:The European Society of Anesthesiology provides guidelines for perioperative fasting in adults and c